-- title:
--   Equivariance of the rigidified dictionary: Γ, Atkin–Lehner, Hecke
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $r$ and $\bar r$ are distinct primes, $N\neq 0$ is squarefree and divisible by neither $r$ nor $\bar r$, and $n\geq 3$ is coprime to $N$ and divisible by neither $r$ nor $\bar r$ (the arithmetic hypotheses `hrr`, `hrN`, `hrbarN`, `hN`, `hn`, `hrn`, `hrbarn`, `hnN`).
--
--   *Base rings.* $\mathcal O$ is a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring, $\pi\in\mathcal O$ is irreducible, $\mathcal O$ is $(\pi)$-adically complete, $\#(\mathcal O/\pi)=r$ and $(r)=(\pi)$; $K_0$ is a characteristic-zero fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Next, $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is a characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$-algebra carrying an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, complete with respect to the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, with that ideal maximal (`hOnr_max`), such that every element of $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial of positive degree over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $\mathrm{Fr}(x)\equiv x^{r}\pmod\pi$ (`hFr`). Write $k_0:=O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)$.
--
--   *Quaternion data.* The pair $a,b\in\mathbb Q$ satisfies `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b r rbar`: $a>0$ or $b>0$, and $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ is a division algebra over the completion at a finite place exactly at the places above $r$ and $\bar r$. Here $\Lambda$ is a maximal order (an order maximal among orders containing it), containing all rational integers (`hΛℤ`), and $\mathrm{coord}\colon\Lambda\to\mathbb Z_{r^2}^{\,2}$, with $\mathbb Z_{r^2}=W(\mathbb F_{r^2})$, satisfies `IsOrderCoord`: additive, sending $1$ to $(1,0)$, multiplicative for the $\varpi$-twisted product law, injective, with dense image in the $r$-adic sense, and compatible with reduced traces. On the definite side, $a_1,b_1$ satisfy `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt rbar` ($a_1<0$, $b_1<0$, ramified exactly at $\bar r$); $\Lambda_1$ is a maximal order, $R_1$ an Eichler order of level $N$ (an intersection of two maximal orders of relative index $N$) with $R_1\leq\Lambda_1$; $\iota_0\colon\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]\to M_2(K_0)$ is an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra map; $v$ is a height-one prime of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ containing $r$; and $\tilde\Gamma$ (`Γt`) is the subgroup of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]^{\times}$ consisting of the units lying in the local unit box of $R_1$ at every prime $w\neq v$.
--
--   *Data on the special fibre.* $A_0$ is a fake elliptic curve over $k_0$ with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure, $X_0$ a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $k_0$ (a two-dimensional formal group with $\mathbb Z_{r^2}$-action and uniformiser endomorphism $\varpi$, $\varpi^2=[r]$, $\varpi\circ[a]=[a^{\sigma}]\circ\varpi$) of height $4$ (`hX₀`), and $\theta_0$ a system of formal coordinates of dimension $2$ along the unit section of $A_0$, with `hA₀` asserting that $\theta_0$ identifies the formal completion of $A_0$ with $X_0$ compatibly with $\mathrm{coord}$. Maps $e,e'\colon\tilde\Gamma\to\mathrm{End}(A_0.A)$ over the base are given, together with $\deg\colon\tilde\Gamma\to\mathbb N$.
--
--   *The endomorphism dictionary (hypotheses `hE1`–`hE4`).* `hE1`: each $(e\gamma,e'\gamma)$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ from $A_0$ to $A_0$ (both respect the group law and the $\Lambda$-action, and both composites are the action of $r^{\deg\gamma}$), and $e\gamma$ preserves the level structure. `hE1mul`: for all $\gamma,\gamma'$ there are $i,j$ with $e(\gamma\gamma')$ followed by the action of $r^{i}$ equal to $e\gamma'$ followed by $e\gamma$ followed by the action of $r^{j}$. `hE1sc`: if $\gamma$ is the central scalar $c\in\mathbb Z$ then $e\gamma$ followed by the action of $r^{i}$ is the action of $c\,r^{i}$, for some $i$. `hE1'`: conversely, if $e\gamma$ followed by the action of some $r^{i}$ equals the action of a positive integer, then $\gamma$ is a rational scalar. `hE2`: for every injective ring homomorphism $E_0'$ from the centralizer of $\{X_0.\mathrm{actEnd}\}\cup\{X_0.\varpi\mathrm{End}\}$ into $M_2(K_0)$ there is one $g\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ such that every $\gamma\in\tilde\Gamma$ admits $\varepsilon$ in that centralizer and $k_\gamma\in\mathbb Z$ with $\varepsilon$ inducing $e\gamma$ on formal coordinates (equality of $\theta_0$-values on nilpotent arguments after truncated evaluation of the power series of $\varepsilon$) and $E_0'(\varepsilon)=r^{k_\gamma}\,g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$. `hE3`: every full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$ admits a labelling $\mathrm{lab}\colon\tilde\Gamma\to\Lambda$ with $e\gamma$ carrying $P_0$ to its translate by $\mathrm{lab}\,\gamma$, with $\mathrm{lab}(\gamma\gamma')-\mathrm{lab}(\gamma')\mathrm{lab}(\gamma)\in n\Lambda$, and with central scalars $c$ sent to $c$ modulo $n\Lambda$. `hE4`: for every algebraically closed field $k$ over $k_0$, every fake elliptic curve $A$ over $k$ presented as a pullback of $A_0$ by $g_A$, and every isogeny pair $(\varphi,\psi)$ of degree $r^{d}$ of $A$ with $\varphi$ preserving the level, there are $\gamma\in\tilde\Gamma$ and $i,j$ with $\varphi$ followed by the action of $r^{i}$ and by $g_A$ equal to $g_A$ followed by $e\gamma$ and by the action of $r^{j}$.
--
--   *The order-level dictionary (`hE5a`–`hE5g`).* $R_2\leq R_1$ is an order (contains $1$, is multiplicatively closed, spans the algebra, finitely generated) such that each element of $R_1$ lies in $R_2$ after multiplication by a suitable power of $r$; $\hat e\colon R_2\to\mathrm{End}(A_0.A)$ is given over the base. `hE5a`: each $\hat e(x)$ respects the group law, commutes with the $\Lambda$-action and preserves the level. `hE5one`, `hE5mul`, `hE5int`: $\hat e(1)$ is the identity, $\hat e(xy)=\hat e(y)$ followed by $\hat e(x)$, and $\hat e$ of a rational integer $m$ is the action of $m$. `hE5c`: $\hat e(\bar x)$ followed by $\hat e(x)$ is the action of $\mathrm{nrd}(x)$ when the latter is the integer $n_x$. `hE5d`: if $x=r^{k}\gamma$ then $e\gamma$ and $\hat e(x)$ agree up to actions by powers of $r$. `hE5e`: for every injective $E_0'$ as above there is one $g\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ simultaneously normalising the germs of all $e\gamma$ ($\gamma\in\tilde\Gamma$) and of all $\hat e(x)$ ($x\in R_2$), matching them with $r^{k}\,g\,\iota_0(\cdot)\,g^{-1}$. `hE5g`: $R_2$ is stable under the main involution.
--
--   *The twin-order dictionary (`hE6a`–`hE6f`).* $\Lambda_1^{s}$ is a second maximal order with $R_1\leq\Lambda_1^{s}$ and $\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_1^{s}=R_1$; $R_2'\leq\Lambda_1^{s}$ is an order with $R_2\leq R_2'$ such that each element of $\Lambda_1^{s}$ lies in $R_2'$ after multiplication by a power of $r$; $\hat e'\colon R_2'\to\mathrm{End}(A_0.A)$ is given over the base, with `hE6a` (group law and $\Lambda$-equivariance), `hE6one`, `hE6mul`, `hE6int`, `hE6c` (as for $\hat e$), `hE6d` ($\hat e'$ restricts to $\hat e$ on $R_2$), `hE6star` (stability of $R_2'$ under the involution), `hE6inj` (injectivity of $\hat e'$), and `hE6f`: if for a prime $q\neq r$ the endomorphism $\hat e'(z)$ kills every $q$-torsion point of $A_0$, then $r^{K}z\in q\Lambda_1^{s}$ for some $K$.
--
--   *Drinfeld's moduli datum.* $\iota\colon\mathbb Z_{r^2}\to O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is a ring map; $\Phi$ is a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$ which is special for the induced structure map (`hΦ`: the zero and one weight spaces of its Lie algebra are complementary invertible submodules) and of height $4$ (`hΦ4`); $M$ is a moduli package over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ satisfying the Zariski sheaf condition `hM`; $\eta$ assigns to each rigidified special formal module over an $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$-algebra with $r$ nilpotent a point of $M$; `hη` has three clauses: on admissible data, equality of $\eta$-values is equivalent to isomorphism; $\eta$ is natural under base change of admissible data; and every point of $M$ comes, after passing to a finite cover by localisations generating the unit ideal, from an admissible rigidified module. $E_0$ maps the centralizer of $\{\Phi.\mathrm{actEnd}\}\cup\{\Phi.\varpi\mathrm{End}\}$ into $M_2(K_0)$, and `hE₀` states that $E_0$ is injective and that for some $m$ the matrices $r^{m}A$ with $A\in M_2(\mathcal O)$ are exactly, up to the stated two inclusions, the values of $E_0$ scaled by $r^{m}$.
--
--   *The bridge.* $\kappa\colon k_0\to O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$ is a ring map compatible with the two quotient maps (`hκ`), and $\beta_0$ is a system of power series which is an isogeny of height $4n_0$ from $\Phi$ to the base change of $X_0$ along $\kappa$ (`hβ₀`).
--
--   *Atkin–Lehner data.* $\bar w$ is a unit of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ with $\mathrm{nrd}(\bar w)=\bar r$ normalising $\tilde\Gamma$ (`hwbar`). Further, $A_{0}^{w}$ is a fake elliptic curve over $k_0$ with maps $a_w,a_w'$ exhibiting it as the Atkin–Lehner quotient of $A_0$ at $\bar r$ (`hALw`: compatibility with the group laws and the $\Lambda$-action, both composites equal to the action of $\bar r$, the kernel of $a_w$ described by the elements $m\in\Lambda$ with $m\bar m\in\bar r\mathbb Z$, and preservation of level), together with $b_w,b_w'$ forming an isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_w}$ from $A_0^{w}$ to $A_0$ (`hBSw`) with $b_w$ preserving level (`hBSwlev`); `hJOINTw` states that for every injective $E_0'$ there is one $g\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ realising simultaneously the $\gamma$-clause of `hE2` and an element $\varepsilon_w$ whose germ on $\theta_0$ is $a_w$ followed by $b_w$ with $E_0'(\varepsilon_w)=r^{k_w'}\,g\,\iota_0(\bar w)\,g^{-1}$.
--
--   *The dictionary $\Xi$.* $\Xi$ assigns to each Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$, each $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi\colon O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent in $B$, and each rigidified curve over $(B,\psi)$ (a fake elliptic curve $E$ over $B$ together with a rigidification: reductions $E_b$, $A_b$ modulo $\pi$ presented as pullbacks of $E$ and of $A_0$, and an isogeny pair $\varphi,\varphi'$ of degree $r^{d}$ between them with $\varphi$ preserving level) a $G$-point of $M$ over $B$, namely a triple consisting of an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to B$, the nilpotence of $r$, and a point of $M$. The hypotheses on $\Xi$ are: `hΞleg`, for $B$ with only trivial idempotents the leg of $\Xi$ is $\mathrm{Fr}^{k}$-twisted from $\psi$ for some $k\in\mathbb Z$; `hΞnat`, naturality under $\mathcal O$-algebra maps $B\to B'$ carrying one rigidified curve to another compatibly; `hΞiso`, invariance of $\Xi$ under isomorphisms of rigidified curves admitting the displayed comparison data ($i_b$, $u_A$ and exponents $i_1,j_1$ making the square of $\varphi$'s commute up to actions by powers of $r$); and `hΞdef`, which for $B$ with trivial idempotents and $r$ nilpotent, and a rigidified curve $x$ whose underlying curve carries formal module data $(X,\theta)$ via $\mathrm{coord}$, produces $j\leq 1$ and a rigidified special formal module $t$ over $B$ with $t.X=X$, with $(\theta_0,\kappa,\beta_0)$-transport relating the rigidification of $x$ to $t$ at level $j$, with $t$ admissible for the $\mathrm{Fr}^{-j}$-twist of $\psi$, and with $\Xi(x)$ equal to the $G$-point built from that twist and $\eta(t)$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exists a single $g_0\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ for which the following three statements hold. In each, $Z$ denotes the central unit of $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ given by the scalar matrix $r$, and `ModuliPackage.G.IsActBy ι Φ η Fr E₀ h x x'` is the relation asserting the existence of an element $\varepsilon$ of the centralizer of $\{\Phi.\mathrm{actEnd}\}\cup\{\Phi.\varpi\mathrm{End}\}$ and of $k,m'\in\mathbb N$ with $E_0(\varepsilon)=r^{k}h^{-1}$, with $\varepsilon$ having kernel of degree $r^{2m'}$, and with $x'$ obtained from $x$ by the $\mathrm{Fr}^{m'-2k}$-twist of the leg together with a local lifting of the points to rigidified data translated by $\varepsilon$.
--
--   (1) *Equivariance for $\tilde\Gamma$.* For every Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with only trivial idempotents, every $\psi\colon O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to B$ over $\mathcal O$ with $\pi$ nilpotent in $B$, every fake elliptic curve $E$ over $B$, every two rigidifications $\rho,\rho'$ of $E$ relative to $A_0$ and $\psi$, and every $\gamma\in\tilde\Gamma$: if $\rho'$ is the translate of $\rho$ by $e\gamma$ (there are comparison maps $u,u_A$ between the two rigidifications and a lift $e_{\gamma b}$ of $e\gamma$ to $\rho.A_b$ with the two composites through $\varphi$ agreeing after the actions of $r^{i}$ and $r^{j}$), then there is $c\in\mathbb Z$ such that $\Xi(E,\rho)$ and $\Xi(E,\rho')$ are related by the action of $Z^{c}\,(g_0\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g_0^{-1})$.
--
--   (2) *Equivariance for the Atkin–Lehner element at $\bar r$.* For every such $B$, $\psi$ and nilpotence datum, with $\bar r$ invertible in $B$, for all fake elliptic curves $E,E_f$ over $B$ and maps $q\colon E\to E_f$, $q'\colon E_f\to E$ exhibiting $E_f$ as the Atkin–Lehner quotient of $E$ at $\bar r$, and all rigidifications $\rho$ of $E$ and $\rho_f$ of $E_f$: if there exist $q_b\colon\rho.E_b\to\rho_f.E_b$ compatible with the $g_b$'s via $q$ and lying over the base, $u_A\colon\rho_f.A_b\to\rho.A_b$ a pullback along the identity with $u_A$ followed by $\rho.g_A$ equal to $\rho_f.g_A$, an endomorphism $e_{wb}$ of $\rho.A_b$ over the base with $e_{wb}$ followed by $\rho.g_A$ equal to $\rho.g_A$ followed by $a_w$ and then $b_w$, and exponents $i,j$ with $q_b$ followed by $\rho_f.\varphi$, $u_A$ and the action of $r^{i}$ equal to $\rho.\varphi$ followed by $e_{wb}$ and the action of $r^{j}$, then there is $c\in\mathbb Z$ with $\Xi(E,\rho)$ and $\Xi(E_f,\rho_f)$ related by the action of $Z^{c}\,(g_0\,\iota_0(\bar w)\,g_0^{-1})$.
--
--   (3) *Equivariance for the Hecke element at $\ell$.* For every adelic unit $n_1$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb A_{\mathbb Q}^{f}$ lying in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$, such that the intersection order $R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ is Eichler of level $Nr$; for every prime $\ell$ distinct from $r$ and $\bar r$, every unit $s$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ and every adelic unit $s_f$ such that $s_f$ has component $s\otimes 1$ at each finite place not containing $r$, component $1$ at the places containing $r$, the product of the diagonal image of $\ell$ with $s_f^{-1}$ lies in the level Hecke set $\mathrm{levelHeckeUSet}\,\Lambda_1\,(R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1})\,\ell$ when $\ell\mid N$ and in the prime Hecke set of $R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ at $\ell$ otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s)=\ell$; and for every extra level-$\ell$ structure $C_0$ on $A_0$, fake elliptic curve $A_0^{s}$ over $k_0$ with maps $a_s,a_s'$ exhibiting $A_0^{s}$ as the $\ell$-level-isogeny quotient of $(A_0,C_0)$, maps $b_s,b_s'$ forming an isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_s}$ from $A_0^{s}$ to $A_0$ with $b_s$ preserving level, and the joint normalisation `hJOINTs` (for every injective $E_0'$ one $g$ realising both the $\gamma$-clause of `hE2` and an element $\varepsilon_s$ whose germ on $\theta_0$ is $a_s$ followed by $b_s$, with $E_0'(\varepsilon_s)=r^{k_s'}\,g\,\iota_0(\bar s)\,g^{-1}$ for the conjugate $\bar s$ of $s$): the following holds. For every Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with only trivial idempotents, every $\psi$ and nilpotence datum as above, with $\ell$ invertible in $B$, every fake elliptic curve with extra level-$\ell$ structure $u$ over $B$, every fake elliptic curve $E'$ over $B$ and maps $q\colon u.1\to E'$, $q'\colon E'\to u.1$ exhibiting $E'$ as the $\ell$-level-isogeny quotient of $u$, and all rigidifications $\rho$ of $u.1$ and $\rho'$ of $E'$: if there exist $q_b$, $u_A$, an endomorphism $e_{sb}$ of $\rho.A_b$ over the base with $e_{sb}$ followed by $\rho.g_A$ equal to $\rho.g_A$ followed by $a_s$ and then $b_s$, and exponents $i,j$ with $q_b$ followed by $\rho'.\varphi$, $u_A$ and the action of $r^{i}$ equal to $\rho.\varphi$ followed by $e_{sb}$ and the action of $r^{j}$, then there is $c\in\mathbb Z$ with $\Xi(u.1,\rho)$ and $\Xi(E',\rho')$ related by the action of $Z^{c}\,(g_0\,\iota_0(\ell s^{-1})\,g_0^{-1})$, where $\ell$ is taken as the central unit coming from $\mathbb Q^{\times}$.
--
--   Thus one and the same conjugator $g_0$ serves for the $\tilde\Gamma$-action, for the Atkin–Lehner element at $\bar r$, and for the Hecke element at every admissible $\ell$, the identifications being valid modulo the central powers of $r$.
--
--   This is the equivariance step of the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison on the supersingular locus: the dictionary $\Xi$, which converts rigidified fake elliptic curves over $\pi$-nilpotent bases into points of Drinfeld's moduli package, is shown to transport translation by $\tilde\Gamma$, the Atkin–Lehner involution at $\bar r$ and the Hecke correspondence at $\ell$ into the action of $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ through a single conjugate of $\iota_0$, up to the central subgroup generated by $r$. It feeds the construction of the $p$-adic uniformisation with fine level, Atkin–Lehner and Hecke structure used downstream.
